# Development Workflow and Best Practices

## Project Setup
- Use `npm run install:all` to install all dependencies
- Use `npm run dev` to start both backend and frontend concurrently
- Backend runs on port 3001, frontend on port 3000

## Code Quality Standards
- Use ESLint configuration from [package.json](mdc:frontend/package.json)
- Follow consistent naming conventions
- Write comprehensive tests for all new features
- Maintain high test coverage

## Git Workflow
- Use feature branches: `git checkout -b feature/amazing-feature`
- Write descriptive commit messages
- Test before committing
- Use conventional commit format when possible

## Environment Configuration
- Use environment variables for configuration
- Default Ollama URL: `http://localhost:11434`
- Default model: `openchat:latest`
- Support for different environments (dev, prod)

## Error Handling Standards
- Always handle async operations with try-catch
- Provide meaningful error messages
- Log errors for debugging
- Graceful degradation for external service failures

## Performance Considerations
- Use streaming for long AI responses
- Implement proper cleanup for resources
- Monitor memory usage with Selenium
- Optimize React re-renders

## Security Best Practices
- Validate all user inputs
- Sanitize URLs before browsing
- Implement rate limiting for production
- Use HTTPS in production

## Documentation
- Keep README.md updated
- Document API endpoints
- Include setup instructions
- Document environment variables

## Testing Strategy
- Unit tests for all business logic
- Integration tests for API endpoints
- Mock external dependencies
- Test error scenarios
- Maintain test coverage reports